Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 11:42:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] R80b, part 4, patch 1 (cld-advisor, at main's word in M14;
 Review 80, the SM seat's finding 36 and the first part of a reader's F12,
 both checked by main on the code): THE LISTENER NAMES EVERY MESSAGE THAT WAS
 READ AND HAS NO RECORD OF ITS TEXT, WHETHER OR NOT A NEW ONE CAME.

WHAT STOOD. A seat's listener shows again a message that main has changed in place, by comparing a record of its text. Where its memory held no record at all and nothing was new, it said so (Review 79's second round). Two cases were still lost. With such a memory and a new message together, the new message was shown, nothing was said of the old ones, and all were stored as read. And a memory that holds a record for some of the messages read and not for others said nothing of the others.

WHAT IS CHANGED. Every message that was read and has no record of its text is named, whether or not a new one came, and the seat is told to read it on the page again. The old condition stands in a dated note.

THE TEST plants both cases in a small repository, and a twin: with a record for every message, a change elsewhere on the page names none. With the listener of the commit before, the test fails on the first case. The file's eight older tests pass. 0 of 19.
---
 scripts/seats/listen.py     | 21 +++++++++++++++------
 tests/test_seat_listener.py | 36 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 51 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

